/* ============================================================================
   8. FOREST ENVIRONMENT  (continuous 2-D world)
   A 22 m x 15 m patch of forest with a 9 m x 9 m building plot in a clearing.
   Learning agents gather a stick and a stone, make an axe (it wears out), chop
   trees into logs, carry each log to the plot and place it by hand. Every log
   is a 1 m wall piece. Where it goes is the agent's choice: straight on, turning
   left, turning right, or leaving a doorway. Quick placement leaves slightly
   loose joints; an agent can spend time tightening the last one.
   When the walls enclose a space the house is finished and scored:
     space inside   (flood fill of the real log geometry)
     insulation     (loose joints and extra openings let the wind in)
     door           (a house needs exactly one doorway)
